  "verdict": "Direction closes. Largest gain over a hardcoded default across 270 trials and three architectures is +0.40 points (model_iter_1094), against a +2 threshold fixed in advance. model_iter_165 was not beaten by any of its 90 trials. Winning configurations land at effective lr 0.1358/0.0991/0.0991 against the default's 0.1000. batch_size folds into the collapse on all three (p=0.41-0.63) as predicted; weight_decay is genuinely independent on all three (p=0.004, surviving Bonferroni, and strengthening to delta R2 +0.23..+0.27 at p=0.002 when orthogonalised against lr) as predicted -- but it is downside-only, the default sitting in its best bin on all three while the top bin costs 16-23 points. model_iter_1094 fails the pre-registered search-adequacy criterion (no plateau by trial 30) and its result is reported as inconclusive on budget grounds rather than as no-headroom."
